<o:Entity Id="o336">
<a:ObjectID>939DC922-FF46-46E2-B4E7-CFD19ED15EF8</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>MATERIAL_TYPE</a:Name>
<a:Code>MATERIAL TYPES</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1587411946</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>TOOLBUS</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1587501685</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Gabriela.Velea</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The definition of an object or good that is identified and measured by quantity, volume, or count.  A Material Type may or may not be uniquely identifiable, but it is not tracked at the individual instance level, as it is not important to the enterprise to track these items at that level.
Examples of MATERIAL TYPES include:  oil, water, gas, computer keyboards, paper clips, 2-3/8&quot; red band 4.7 lb/ft tubing, 2-7/8&quot; yellow band 6.5 lb/ft tubing, Milwaukee size 3 cast iron 200 psig working pressure butterfly valve, John Crane 5611 1-3/4&quot; Cartridge mount Mechanical Seal.</a:Comment>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{C6AC31EB-C90E-4811-BE11-ED1545ECDA32},SHL_CDM_EntityPropertyExtension,351={4E82BA4A-68B2-4115-B5EA-3B441E3475E3},MTED_EDaM_Entity_Data_Category,13=&lt;unspecified&gt;
