<o:Entity Id="o362">
<a:ObjectID>AF8923F6-2A5E-4D13-871C-08ABDA3F986C</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>WORK_ACTIVITY</a:Name>
<a:Code>WORK ACTIVITIES</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1587411946</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>TOOLBUS</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1587501685</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Gabriela.Velea</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The carrying out of Work.  It may be as high-level as a program or as detailed as a task.  A Work Activity requires inputs (resources, e.g. persons, rigs, cement) and produces an output (e.g. a facility, a well, a drawing, a weld).  It tracks usage and consumption of resources involved in the work. It may fulfill a work request or work order.  Activities exist to carry out / build / upgrade / fix / maintain / order / measure / test, etc. Work Activities may be grouped together across Projects or WBS Elements to ensure optimum resource useage or to minimze the impact of the work (for example, in the case of a maintenance campagn, aligning shutdown windows to minimize deferment, leveling the use of shared resources to minimize cost, etc).</a:Comment>
<a:Annotation>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Segoe UI;}}
\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\f0\fs20 *** PURPOSE:\par
Q - typicals, e.g. templates, e.g. plant maintenance.  Given how much they have in common, should Work Procedures (typicals) also be captured here? &quot;We did good work, let&#39;s do that again.  Could mark it immediately as a best practice without needing to copy it elsewhere first.&quot;\par
}</a:Annotation>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{C6AC31EB-C90E-4811-BE11-ED1545ECDA32},SHL_CDM_EntityPropertyExtension,344={4E82BA4A-68B2-4115-B5EA-3B441E3475E3},MTED_EDaM_Entity_Data_Category,13=&lt;unspecified&gt;
